WEBVTT

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.150
You may not believe me, but...

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.020
...even before he told me his name...

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.940
...I felt as if...

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.530
...I already knew who he was.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.070
Yano... Motoharu.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.670
I'm Takahashi Nanami.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.500
This is my second day of high school.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.420
It'd be nice if I could make lots of friends.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.430
F-For now, I'll try to...

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:00.470
U-Umm... I'm Takahashi Nanami.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.430
N-Nice to meet you.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.140
I'm Yamamoto Yuri. Nice to meet you.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.150
U-Umm, what middle school are you from?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.100
Asahi.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.360
Ah... we have to change classrooms for home ec, right? Can I go with you guys?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.610
Ah, you were in the first seat in the front, right?

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.160
Yeah. I'm Takahashi Nanami.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:19.780
What middle school are you from?

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.570
South.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.740
We're both from West.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:25.200
There don't seem to be any girls in our class from Asahi, huh?

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.710
Ah, this girl Yamamoto-san who sits next to me is from Asahi Middle School.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:30.880
No way! You talked to her?

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:31.880
You must've heard a lot about him.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:32.960
About who?

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.380
Motoharu!

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.090
Who...?

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.970
We were with Motoharu during the winter session, and he's just so cool!

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.680
He was popular with both the girls and guys.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.850
They even say that in his last year of middle school...

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.440
...two-thirds of the girls in class were in love with him at the same time!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.150
So someone like that is in the same class as me...

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:59.780
Ah, hey, you're from the same middle school as Yano-kun, right?

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:00.400
Yeah.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.910
I heard two-thirds of the girls fell for him?

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.910
I hate him.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.910
Hey, Nana, wanna be on the class committee?

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.920
Ah... I prefer an easy life, so...

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.920
I really wanna be with Motoharu on the committee...

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.880
What's the procedure for joining it? Do you get nominated?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.470
Though announcing it by yourself is kinda lame...

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.720
How about I nominate you?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.590
Will you really?

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.180
Sure.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.510
Er... what was her name again...?

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.310
Mizu... Mizu something...

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.310
I'll be counting on you!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.810
A-Ah, yeah!

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.890
I can't possibly ask her...

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:36.230
U-Umm, what was that girl's name again...?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.900
Mizu... Mizu...

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.160
Mizuhara.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.660
You may not believe me, but...

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.670
...even before he told me his name...

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.210
... I felt as if...

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.170
... I already knew who he was.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.670
Yano Motoharu.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.300
Be the class president.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.550
I was right...

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.430
Don't you think this nomination's a little arbitrary?

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.470
But nobody nominated anyone else or nominated themselves, so...

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:11.140
I'll nominate someone. I nominate myself as <i>vice</i> president.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.640
There you go, taking the easy way out again...

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.900
Vice President Yano-kun, huh?

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.480
Ah... umm, I'd also like to nominate someone...

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.490
...for the role of secretary, Mizuhara-san.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.620
Did you mean Mizuguchi-san?

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:37.880
So in the end, I ended up as class president...

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.630
That was pretty rude of you.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.710
You lied to me before, didn't you?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:45.090
Ahh... was I more rude than forgetting someone's name?

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.850
This guy is kind of annoying...

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.850
But isn't it really my fault for forgetting her name...?

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.600
So, um... you...

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.600
What was your name again?

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.320
Hey, I wonder if Yano-kun's had a girlfriend before...

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.030
I've heard he's gone out with a lot of different girls...

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.570
Both younger and older!

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.530
Seriously?

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.370
I dunno. They're just rumors.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.040
Let's try asking Yamamoto-san!

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.580
It seems like I'm a part of the other third of the class...

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.290
Don't ask me about him. I don't know. Not interested in the least.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.800
She said she didn't know...

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.340
Friends.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:25.930
Moron?

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.300
High school...

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.020
...isn't as fun as I thought it'd be.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.650
Nana, did you finish your career counseling session?

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.270
Yeah.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.400
How was it?

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.610
Umm... I didn't understand it very much...

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.900
What's up with that?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:43.530
See ya!

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.320
Bye bye.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.450
I wonder if I should've joined a club, too...

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.570
Takahashi!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.080
How long did your career counseling session last?

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:55.750
Seven minutes.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:56.710
Seven minutes?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.670
Ten minutes.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.330
No, it took half an hour.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.710
Seriously, it took only five minutes.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.250
Just kidding, it took fifteen.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.050
Moron?

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.920
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:07.680
Bye bye.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:11.350
Bye--

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.350
Umm, bye by--

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.520
What?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.610
I... I thought you didn't hear me, so...

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:26.820
Bye... bye bye...

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.030
Why...?

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:36.540
Bye bye.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.500
No, no! This isn't my heart beating faster for him... he only surprised me.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.050
I just didn't think he'd call out to me like that.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.760
That's why... that's why...

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:48.630
What's your problem?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:54.930
I... I just don't understand Math I at all, and I was getting frustrated.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.390
What? You plan on using math down you career path?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.560
N-No, I plan to go to a liberal arts private school...

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.440
Then why bother worrying about the sciences?

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.480
Don't you think it'd be wiser to use this time focusing on liberal arts instead?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.820
But... when you're so bad at something, then...

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:10.280
Even if you're bad at it, nothing will come from it.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.490
It won't help you at all.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.200
I don't understand why people do useless things they don't even like.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.990
Hey! I heard the week after next is a school trip?

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:18.200
But we have tests before that...

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.000
I don't know what I'm gonna do. I haven't studied at all.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.710
Gonna be a piece of cake for you, Nana?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:26.090
No way, I've practically given up. I'll probably get a zero or something in math.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.130
A zero, huh?

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:33.300
Amazing... I actually got a zero...

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.260
Takahashi.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:35.970
Yes?!

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.600
We should probably decide who's in charge of the trip soon...

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.350
Ah... the people to head the teams, yeah...

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:41.350
And about buying stuff for the trip...

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.020
Ah, yeah? About buying stuff?

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.110
It's a pain, so can you go with the girls to take care of it?

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.940
Sure, sur- huh?! Why?!

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.530
I can see that, you know.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.290
This is... umm...! I just wasn't feeling well, so...

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.910
I'd like you and the girls to take care of the shopping...

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.830
No! Why do we always get the annoying stuff?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.590
Hey, guys, amazing stuff! Takahashi's math grade was...

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:10.460
We'll go! We'll go!

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:11.050
Thank you.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.310
Don't be tricked, don't be tricked.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.570
Even if he smiled like that, it's just because he threatened to blurt out your math grade...

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.650
You can't go on to the next grade with a failing mark...

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:36.450
But Yamamoto-san, didn't you say to drop math if I was aiming for liberal arts school?

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.030
But a failing grade is no good, obviously.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:46.920
How should I put this... there are times when you begin to hate everything around you.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.130
It's Yano...

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.760
W-What's up with my heart thumping like that?!

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.990
What are you doing?

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:16.910
Ah... I wanted to look at the sky, so...

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.910
Because of that zero, right?

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.240
Did you get the same...?

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.200
Me? I got an 87.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.330
What's up with that?

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.040
But anyway, do you really think it's worth worrying about?

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.170
I wonder...

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:36.260
Yeah. Everyone is good at something. Isn't it all right if you just try your best at that?

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.510
And besides, don't you think getting a zero's pretty impressive in another way?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.310
Have a seat.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:49.190
Yano, is there anything you're not good at?

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:49.900
Me?

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.110
Next to nothing, I bet.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:51.860
There is!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:52.730
You're lying.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:53.820
There is, there is.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.570
I'm too popular with the girls.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:57.990
Are you stupid?

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.200
What?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.700
Besides that, do you have trouble with anything else?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:06.830
Yeah.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:10.330
I stand out, so I'm always being watched.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.300
And even though it's annoying, I normally get picked to be on the class committee.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:15.960
I can't sleep at night.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:21.090
And I hate... fickle girls.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.810
That makes five! Yay!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.850
Hey... none of those are problems.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.820
And when you say "fickle", do you really have the right to talk that way about others?

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:35.940
What? Are you making fun of me?

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.650
Despite my looks, I'm pretty single-minded.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:39.450
Don't I seem that way?

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.160
Not at all.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:49.370
I wonder what kind of girls Yano falls for...

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:57.010
Hey.. if the girl you were going out with was fickle, what would you do?

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:02.550
I wonder why I want to know his answer...

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:04.810
Yano?

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.310
I'd kill her.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:12.690
Just kidding.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:20.650
I'm not sure why I asked...

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:24.620
Yano, if you have any problems, I'll lend an ear.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:33.330
Well... about anything. You just listened to me go on, so...

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.340
That's too bad. I don't have any problems.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.670
There's that smile again...

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:43.840
I don't believe this is happening...

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:48.270
This is definitely going to be the worst mistake of my life...

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:54.020
Yano... I like--

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.270
Oh, and about your problems...

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:57.860
That's a right reserved for the living, don't you think?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.370
Well... yes...

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:24.430
At that moment... I didn't know what Yano meant when he said that.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:29.720
Uh... umm...

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.390
Take note of these important points during our walkathon school trip.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.730
We will travel by bus to the starting point.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:38.730
The entire length is 42 km, and... hey, Yano!

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.860
Explain this important stuff to everyone!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.360
The use of cell phones is prohibited.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.990
And no shopping at any shops along the path!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.450
Oh, Take.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.450
No using you cell phone.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.200
O-Okay.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.700
How was that?

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:55.960
Geez... I feel so pathetic, falling for someone incredibly irresponsible like him...

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:00.390
Ah, we're here!

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:01.430
I'm going to collect everyone's cell phones now!

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.930
I don't have one.

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:04.930
Does he really not have one...?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.140
What's with that grin...?

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:09.350
I'm telling you, I forgot to bring it.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.690
What? Yano really doesn't have one with him?

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.730
Ah, it's so nice out!

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.110
This might actually be fun!

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:16.700
I wonder if we'll be able to make it the whole 42 km...

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:20.950
Heh, really?

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:23.290
Nana, talk to him for us!

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.080
Me?

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.080
Well, you have a relationship with him since you're prez and he's vice prez.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.710
Please! I'm counting on you!

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:31.790
Ah... I guess I have no choice, huh?

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.180
Ah, hey...

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:39.050
Motoharu!

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:45.140
W-Want to have lunch together, Yamamoto-san?

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:47.390
What are you doing, inviting Yamamoto-san...?

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:48.270
Get Yano, too!

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.650
My timing was off...

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:52.770
You don't want to eat with Yamamoto-san?

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.940
Well, it's not that we don't want to, she's just hard to talk to.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.860
She gives off a dark aura...

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:00.410
D-Don't say that.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:03.580
Well, it's just fine and all... but be sure to invite Yano and the others, too.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:04.370
Okay.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:07.500
I hate him.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.040
Oh no, what am I gonna do?

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.750
If I invite Yano now, it'll be like I did it to harass Yamamoto-san...

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:19.760
Even though almost nobody hates him, I wonder why Yamamoto-san does...

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.680
Hey... who's that person?

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:25.560
Ah, that's Takeuchi-kun.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:27.810
Apparently, they were both in same class in middle school.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:30.190
Even now, they still seem to hang out a lot.

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.190
It's the half way point!

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:34.400
That went by fast!

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:35.690
Think you'll be able to walk the whole 42 km?

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.980
Yeah. Piece of cake.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.030
We did it!

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:39.740
Yeah!

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:41.240
Yano.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:45.490
W... Want to eat lunch with everyone?

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:49.160
Ah, sure, but... can you keep up with our pace?

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.710
Ah... I'm starting to get tired...

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.920
The scenery isn't changing a bit, either...

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:57.000
I'm starting to get bored of nature.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.460
We should've retired at the 20 km mark...

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.510
Hey... wanna sit down for lunch now?

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.720
I'm exhausted.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:04.850
Yeah...

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:07.310
In the end, we lost track of Yano and the others, anyway...

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:08.640
Yamamoto-san?

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:11.730
Are you all right?

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.810
Want some water?

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.900
Huh? What's the matter?

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:17.020
Takeuchi-kun.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.150
She's not feeling well...

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:21.530
Do you think the teachers will pass by in their cars?

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:25.820
Ah... I think they're eating lunch at the cabin back at the 20 km halfway point...

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.580
They should be by in an hour or two.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.290
An hour or two, huh?

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:32.500
For now, if I find someone who can get in touch with them, I'll let them know.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:33.290
Thanks.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:36.130
Yamamoto-san, can you eat some fruit?

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:37.290
It might refresh you...

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:40.380
I brought some cold juice with me...

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.300
What are we gonna do?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.930
I wonder if she'll get better if she takes a break...

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.930
I wonder if we have to wait for the teachers...

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:52.480
This is no good... I'm the one who's supposed to be responsible, but I can't do anything to help...

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:53.890
Huh? Someone's heading back this way.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.690
It's Yano.

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:57.400
Huh? Why?

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:59.400
Take got in touch with me.

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:00.820
Got in touch with him?

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:02.940
Hey. Did you eat breakfast?

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.530
Do you have any symptoms of dehydration?

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.030
Did you try licking some salt?

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:06.740
Do you have a fever?

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:15.830
She has a fever.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.960
No way! What'll we do?

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.590
We should get someone with a car to come over here.

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:21.840
But how will we contact the teachers?

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:25.930
Ah, it's me. Where are you right now?

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:27.300
About 25 km in?

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:29.600
How long before you reach the goal?

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:30.600
Another two hours?

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.600
The teachers haven't passed by yet, right?

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.890
Ah, okay.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.560
I'm going to return to the halfway point.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.230
The halfway point?

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:40.650
They're eating lunch in the barbecue house at the lodge back there.

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:43.990
If I go now to get them, they can be back here in five minutes if they drive.

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:45.360
You guys stay here.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.870
Hey, do any of you have your cell phones with you?

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:51.030
None of us... they were taken away.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.040
Huh? How about you two?

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.290
No...

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:55.040
I don't have mine.

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.790
Why can't you girls keep control of your own cell phones?

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.790
"Why?"

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.000
I have mine...

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:06.170
I have mine... so we'll be fine...

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:07.970
No way...

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:10.890
Ah, I'll come with you.

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:12.350
It's fine. You stay behind.

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.930
But I'm pretty much the responsible party here, so...

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:17.190
If you start slowing me down, I'll leave you behind.

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.900
Your number hasn't changed, right?

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:34.410
They know each other's cell phone numbers because they were in the same class in middle school, right?

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.710
Why are you walking like a snail? I'll seriously leave you behind.

00:17:37.710 --> 00:17:38.670
Yeah...

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:44.170
Ah... I'm such a bad person... worrying about something else when Yamamoto-san is like that...

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:48.880
Hey, were you close to Yamamoto-san in middle school?

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.970
Not really. She hardly talked to me.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.720
She's been pretty quiet since a long time ago.

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.180
I see...

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:58.270
So she's been like that since long ago...

00:17:58.270 --> 00:17:59.390
What do you mean, "like that"?

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:05.610
Well, she doesn't really express her feelings... I wonder if she's a single child?

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:07.780
She isn't.

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:08.990
She had an older sister.

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:11.530
Really?

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:13.620
Er... huh? Past tense?

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:16.870
Ah, yeah. She died last summer.

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:22.630
I had no idea...

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.670
Isn't it better that way?

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.760
She seems like the type who would hate being pitied.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.970
How'd she die?

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.140
It was a car accident.

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:35.850
Yano... did you go to the funeral?

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:36.850
No.

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:41.270
It was summer vacation, after all

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:49.150
I've... never experienced anything like that, so I don't really understand, but...

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:52.110
It must be really difficult, huh?

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:54.820
Probably...

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:02.790
I'm... really an unsympathetic girl...

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:08.300
Even though we're having this discussion, my heart's beating really fast because of Yano...

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:10.090
Yamamoto?

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:11.970
It looks like she came down with a fever.

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:15.220
The 25 km point, huh?

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:15.850
Yeah.

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:17.850
Then, Sensei, I'm counting on you.

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:20.350
Ah, yes. I haven't had any beer, so I should be fine.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:23.100
H-Hey, shouldn't we go with him?

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:24.850
There's nothing more we can do, right?

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.360
Let's just leave the rest to him.

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:30.360
Two plates of beef ribs and two Oolong teas, please!

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:31.900
I'm amazed at you...

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.860
They say one should be efficient in life, right?

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:37.490
Ah... and some cow tongue and barbecued beef giblets too, please.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:38.990
Well... whatever.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:41.330
Yano.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:44.580
Today...

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:47.380
It really helped that you were here...

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.800
Th-Thanks.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:59.640
I've never seen someone with as carefree a smile as his...

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:05.650
Ah, you're late! What were you doing?

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:08.230
Yamamoto-san was taken home by the teacher.

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:09.730
Looks like it was just the common cold.

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.360
Is that so? Thank goodness.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:17.990
Umm... buses will be leaving from all over, so please make sure you board the right one.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.080
Understand?

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:28.920
Even though we just parted from each other... I want to see him again...

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.380
Takeuchi-kun.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.180
Yeah.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:39.010
Thanks for before. It really helped.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:40.560
Ah, how did things turn out?

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:45.770
Well, we got a teacher to come by in a car and take her home.

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:47.310
Really? That's good to hear.

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:51.230
I was just thinking you were all so great, thinking on behalf of your friends.

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.110
Huh, really?

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:55.820
Well... a lot's happened, so...

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:57.950
A lot?

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.990
She died last summer.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.240
Yeah... I guess so...

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.330
So you heard about it...

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:06.960
Yeah.

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:09.290
It must be hard, huh?

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:11.460
Yeah... if it were me, I wouldn't be able to get back up...

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.920
R-Really...?

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:20.600
No one close to me has died yet, so I don't really get it, but I wonder how it must feel...

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.100
I wonder if a person would just put a stopper on their life...

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:26.230
Though, I feel like they're a different type of person...

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:30.480
Yeah... but you can't just tell from their outward appearance, so...

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:32.770
Yeah...

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.650
But, really... it's kind of bad...

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:36.530
Really?

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:37.240
Yeah.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:45.450
I've never seen them cry before... and I think it'd be better if they'd just cry or let it distract them...

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:49.460
But I have no idea if they're over it, or if they're still saddened about it...

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:52.920
...or something else entirely... I just don't know.

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.210
It's really scary.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:56.460
You don't have to talk about them like that!

00:21:57.340 --> 00:22:01.470
Saying they're "scary". I think they're really strong.

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:03.430
Well, yeah, but...

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:08.480
I think it's okay not to keep it all bottled up sometimes.

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:12.940
It can be really frustrating because you're friends, don't you think?

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:16.780
Takeuchi-kun, you're really that close...?

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:20.990
Huh? Even though we're in different classes, we're still friends, right?

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:24.330
Hey...

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:27.870
Who are you talking about...?

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:33.540
Good morning!

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:34.500
Morning.

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.880
You're sunburnt.

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:37.050
I want to peel it all off...

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:39.590
Nice face you have there.

00:22:39.590 --> 00:22:42.180
What? Is that something you normally say to a girl?

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:44.180
How about "that's quite a face".

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:51.440
He's so shameless, stuck-up, irresponsible, and impossible to deal with, but...

00:22:52.650 --> 00:22:55.150
I love him a whole lot...

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:57.650
What is it?

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:10.710
Yamamoto-san's older sister, right?

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:12.370
Yeah. That's why.

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:15.340
It's nothing.

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:20.590
She died last summer.

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:22.590
Probably...

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:25.510
You big liar.

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:30.980
She was... Yano's girlfriend.
